    "granted_by": "Maintainer decision, 2026-08-22. 'GO for Recovery Continuation Attempt 3. The paid-readiness review is closed. The clean f30970e baseline, five-leaf transport, 25-input multi-repo staging, strict staged-byte Stage-1 import, search-free continuation path, current harness closure, and $16.7456 derived hard ceiling are sufficient. No additional canary, rehearsal, storage work, science change, or Stage-1 rerun is authorized.' Against last tested implementation 1833b7a, with f30970e as the follow-up state commit; the two differ only in logs/current_state.json, which is not a harness file, so the tested tree and the pre-authorization HEAD carry the same continuation harness digest. Since attempt 2 one closure landed and was accepted: LEAF TRANSPORT. Attempt 2 died staging the first 1.110 GiB Stage-1 leaf by scp against a 600 s hard-coded per-asset timeout, which needs 1.99 MB/s sustained against a dev box observed at 0.44-0.79 MB/s; failure was arithmetic rather than luck. The slow half has been moved off the paid path entirely: the five leaves were published at $0 from the dev box to the private AlphaAvatar/aadistill-transport repo and the pod now pulls them at hub speed through the ordinary declared-manifest relay contract. RelayInput carries its repository, SESSION_RELAY_INPUTS serializes it, the shared setup fetches each item from its own declared repo and fails closed on an item that declares none, and the $0 precheck groups declared inputs by repository and lists every one. Room was made by retiring 8.4752 GiB of REMOTE relay copies whose canonical local originals were hash-verified first -- a remote retention change, not a retirement of science -- after the Hugging Face private-storage limit was measured to be account-wide rather than per-repository. Re-verified at $0 in this session against the current tree: full suite 2160 passed / 12 skipped in 19:34; frozen-asset verifier passed with no problems; canonical local leaves 5/5 matched and shard_matched; remote 15/15 sizes with the five LFS OIDs equal to the recorded sha256; transport manifest verified true with an empty problem list; 25 relay inputs resolving 0-missing across both repositories; local assets reduced to 2 totalling 1.577 MiB; pricing reproduced from the tree at expected 904.44 minutes; provider holding zero pods.\n\nCovers: One (1) launch of the AutoInitializer Phase-A RECOVERY CONTINUATION, attempt 3, on a single NVIDIA L40S at no more than $0.99/h. It imports the verified Attempt-12 Stage-1 result -- the five preserved selected leaves, in the committed selected order, re-identified from the bytes that actually arrive on the pod -- and runs recovery Stages 2 through 5 under the frozen science, the existing watchdog, soft-stop, hard-stop, artifact-gate and provider-confirmed teardown behaviour. The reviewed execution path is preserved exactly: Stage 0 attestation, strict Stage-1 import, canonical-control measurement once on the frozen Stage-1 suite, admit_leaves over the five imported leaves plus the measured control, device handoff and headroom gate, then frozen recovery Stages 2-5 only, with the conditional seed-sc rung firing only if the frozen rule fires. The five leaves travel as 15 relay inputs from the private transport repository; only 2 small artifacts totalling 1.577 MiB remain on the scp path. Authorized pricing is DERIVED from continuation_budget(), not written: expected $14.9233, per-launch hard ceiling $16.7456, which is also the hard cap. The beam search is not run, not reconstructed, and is structurally unreachable from this harness.\n\nCumulative spend at approval $213.7203 against a cumulative cap of $234.00.\n\nDoes NOT authorize: A beam search, a fresh Stage 1, or any reconstruction of the search - the continuation imports Attempt 12's result and cannot reach a search. Re-ranking or re-selecting the five leaves, or changing their committed selected order. Retraining the permanent controls. Measuring the canonical control more than once, or on anything other than the frozen Stage-1 suite. Any retry after a failure: a failed authorization, transport, staging, imported-leaf, control-measurement, admission, device-handoff, recovery, artifact-integrity, budget or provider gate is a fail-closed stop for review, never an interactive repair on the live pod. Modifying the provider-resilience machinery, the transport manifest, the relay contract or the frozen science during the live run. Any additional canary, rehearsal, storage-reclamation, measurement, readiness, architecture or pricing phase. Any follow-on or automatically started session. Reopening the frozen science: science plan 02be33b9, session plan 9377a2dc, Stage-3 protocol 250f72ef, equivalence interval 0.011695296982299022, feasibility floor 0.3, tokenizer 7781771acc3798ee, recovery fingerprint ab0d8cfd, the seed and conditional-sc policy, the operator ids and declared mathematics, or the recovery, search and selection rules. Reusing the spent attempt-1 or attempt-2 grant or authorization. Deleting any of the 32 sole-copy remote objects totalling 69.671 GiB, including the e1_scaling_20260801 group, or the two protected wheelhouses. Any other paid session. Treating the remaining cumulative headroom as authorization beyond this one launch.\n\nGrant document: logs/autoinit_recovery_continuation_attempt3_grant.json sha256 4bb4f50ebf1b70d9bd8bdcab9c9f5cb918aff3efeae8cf0489494ad2531acba5",
